    {
      "id": "evidence-001-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "16, 16 and 27 variable assignments enumerated with NO pruning and no early exit -- the point being that an exhausted search space and an unsearched one are the same output unless the count is reported, and that a space over the cap is an ERROR here rather than a silent `no`. The counterexample databases are 1 and 2 facts. Note what this does NOT use: the negative direction never appeals to Chandra-Merlin's converse (containment implies a homomorphism), which needs an infinite domain, because a concrete finite database separating the two queries refutes the containment on its own.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
